eshape their emergent behaviour."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Focused ion beam fabrication allows us to sculpt single crystals directly into devices with arbitrary geometries and architectures. This freedom lets our scientific imagination lead the experiment, and enables us to ask new, creative questions: can we unlock new responses by breaking symmetries, select the handedness of an ordered state, or even drive materials into new electronic phases?"}],["$","p",null,{"children":["We welcome enquiries from prospective students, postdoctoral researchers and visitors. If you are interested in joining the group, please ",["$","a",null,{"href":"/join-us.html","style":{"textDecoration":"underline","textUnderlineOffset":"3px"},"children":"get in touch"}],"."]}]]}]]}]]}],["$","footer",null,{"children":["$","div",null,{"className":"footer-row","children":["$","span",null,{"children":"Nanosculpted Quantum Materials · Birch Lab · University of Warwick"}]}]}]]]
